# CLAUDE.md — {{projectName}}

Frappe Framework ticketing project scaffolded by `dude` (stack: `frappe`).
{{#if withHelpdesk}}Frappe Helpdesk provides the ticketing UI; the custom app
`apps/ticketing/` extends it.{{/if}}

## Architecture

- **Local runtime** — Docker Compose: `mariadb`, `redis-cache`, `redis-queue`
  and a `bench` container. On first boot `docker/init.sh` creates the bench
  (`frappe-bench/`, persisted in the `bench_home` volume), the site
  (`$SITE_NAME` from `.env`), installs {{#if withHelpdesk}}Helpdesk and {{/if}}every
  custom app found under `apps/`, then runs `bench start`.
- **Custom apps** — live in `apps/` in this repo and are symlinked into the
  bench in editable mode. Edit on the host; the dev server reloads.
- **`apps/ticketing/`** — the example app. Its README maps every Frappe
  concept (DocType, controller, hooks, tasks, workflow, portal page, API) to
  a concrete file. Follow its patterns when adding features.

## Rules that matter here

- `dude lint` enforces the structural conventions described in
  `.claude/rules/{APP,DT,PY}/` — read the matching rule before fixing a
  violation, and keep new code compliant:
  - **APP** — app layout and `hooks.py` integrity (dotted paths must resolve,
    fixtures declared ↔ shipped).
  - **DT** — DocType conventions (controller + tests present, permissions
    declared, snake_case fieldnames).
  - **PY** — Python safety (no guest-exposed whitelisted methods, no
    interpolated SQL).
- New DocTypes: create them via the Desk UI with developer mode on (the JSON
  is written back into the app), or copy
  `apps/ticketing/ticketing/ticketing/doctype/ticket_escalation_rule/` as a
  starting point. Always keep `<name>.json`, `<name>.py`, `__init__.py` and a
  `test_<name>.py` together.
- Anything that changes the schema or fixtures needs `dude site migrate`
  (or restart: `docker/init.sh` migrates on boot).
- Python in `apps/` is formatted with **ruff** (tabs, Frappe style) —
  `dude format`.

## Commands

`dude help` prints the live catalog. Highlights: `dude up/down/logs/shell`,
`dude bench <raw args>`, `dude site migrate/console/backup/clear-cache/mariadb`,
`dude app new/install`, `dude test`, `dude lint`, `dude format`, `dude docs`{{#if withIac}},
`dude iac …` (Terraform / AWS ECS Fargate — see `iac/README.md`){{/if}}.

Custom project commands can be added under `.dude/commands/` (one file = one
command; see `.dude/commands/README.md`).
